### 2026-08-25 - Add the article extraction module and its fixture tests (commit 3c69185)

**What changed:** Added `spike/extract.js` with `SELECTORS` and
`extractArticleMeta(doc)`. Replaced the smoke test in `spike/extract.test.mjs`
with a loop that runs one test per article entry in `manifest.json`, plus a test
that an empty document returns nulls and does not throw. Corrected the title row
in `spike/README.md` from `og.title` to `og:title`.

**Why:** The README table is the human record of the read paths. `sources` is the
machine record: `extractArticleMeta` returns the label of the path that supplied
each field, so a later fixture test can assert which fallback fired, not only the
value. The two records must agree, and the title row disagreed by one character.
The colon is the real distinction: `og:title` is the `property` attribute value
that `meta[property="og:title"]` selects on, and `og.title` selects nothing.

**Files:** `spike/extract.js` (new), `spike/extract.test.mjs`, `spike/README.md`,
`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-16-milestone-0.md`, `changes.log`.

